{"name":"Embrace","hex":"#e8b8a7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"embrace","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To clasp (someone or each other) in the arms with affection; to take in the arms; to hug.","To seize (something) eagerly or with alacrity; to accept or take up with cordiality; to welcome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of putting arms around someone and bringing the person close to the chest; a hug.","An enclosure partially or fully surrounding someone or something."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/embrace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hug","blocks":[{"text":"A hug is a form of endearment, found in virtually all human communities, in which two or more people put their arms around the neck, back, under the armpits or waists of one another and hold each other closely. If more than two people are involved, it may be referred to as a group hug."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Wedding_hugs.jpg/330px-Wedding_hugs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hug"},{"title":"Acceptance","blocks":[{"text":"Acceptance in psychology is a person's recognition and assent to the finality of a situation without attempting to change or protest it. This plays out at both the individual and societal level as people experience change."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acceptance"},{"title":"Embrace (English band Embrace album)","blocks":[{"text":"Embrace is the eponymously titled sixth studio album by English alternative rock band Embrace. The album, produced by vocalist Richard McNamara, was released on 25 April 2014 in Friday-release countries and on 28 April 2014 in the United Kingdom by independent record label Cooking Vinyl. The album was the band's first in eight years, after the release of their fifth studio album This New Day in 2006."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cf/Embrace_-_Embrace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embrace_(English_band_Embrace_album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG/500px-A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG/1280px-A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG/500px-A_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Yoruba bride and mother","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Yoruba_bride_and_mother.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg/500px-2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg/1280px-2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg/500px-2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_%2836352501196%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Two men hug after a volleyball match in Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2017-08-04-Paul_Reimer-Beach_Volleyball_Medals-043_(36352501196).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Cri